7	 * ONE of them (`GROUP BY … LIMIT 1`, no ORDER BY) and pins that one. When it
8	 * returns the row that is already correctly pinned, the pin UPDATE no-ops — its
9	 * WHERE requires `device_worker_id IS DISTINCT FROM target` — and the sibling
10	 * stays bound to a worker that will never poll again. Nothing revisits it.
11	 *
12	 * Silent since #2286 stopped the 23505 crash: no error, just a connection
13	 * pointing at a vanished Mac, claimable by nobody.
